
KEY INSIGHTS

1. Customer Analysis
The bank has 500 customers across different customer segments.
Student (99) and Business (97) are the two largest customer segments.
Account activity, balances and card usage vary across customer segments.

2. Account Analysis
Out of 700 accounts, 497 are active (approximately 71%).
IRA accounts have the highest total balance among the account types in the dashboard.
Account balances and activity vary across account types and branches.

3. Transaction Analysis
The dataset contains 5,000 transactions.
Interest transactions have the highest total transaction amount (approximately ₹6.4 million), followed by Credit transactions (approximately ₹6.3 million).
Monthly transaction amounts vary, with August showing the highest amount (approximately ₹3.34 million) in the displayed trend.

4. Loan Analysis
The bank has 300 loans, with a total loan amount of ₹72.21 million and an outstanding balance of ₹53.44 million.
Out of 2,000 loan-payment records, 500 have a delay, representing 25% of payment records.
Education loans have the highest loan amount and outstanding balance among the loan types shown.

5. Card Analysis
The dataset contains 600 cards, of which 37 are marked as active.
The dashboard shows both Credit and Debit cards, with more inactive than active cards.
Card type, network, credit limits and reward points provide further information about card engagement.
